hello everyone and welcome to the pod on  today's episode we are joined by graeme  jennings who is the senior producer  behind hyperscape  and we're also joined by tanner slaves  who is not only a part of the very first  hyper escape twitch rivals tournament  but also placed second in this past  weekend's 50 thousand dollar  creator cup they're going to be helping  us break down hyperscape from the very  first things you should be learning  all the way to high level tournament  plays let's get to it  hyperscape is officially available  everywhere but  some players are still dropping in for  the very first time so graeme can you  give us some tips on what players should  be learning  first and what the most important thing  is when you are dropping into the  hyperscape i think the key things for  players for the first time they play is  really  you want to land close to where your  lobby is so basically  the games split out into four lobbies at  the game start so you want to land on a  point that's fairly low  and close to you that will allow you to  get there first and you're likely to  have less opposition  from there you want to quickly look for  a weapon so you can smash the barricades  with your battle and start to look for a  weapon you want to pick up a weapon  early  secondly to that we have the function  called hacks they're basically abilities  for players to be able to use  it's good to pick up a hack quickly as  well things like  teleport invisibility slam or things  that add to your movement to keep you  safe in the early game so you need to  make sure you're armed early and you  need to make sure you have a hack with  you as well  and from your point of view tanner what  are some tournament tips you can give  for those players who are trying to get  those next level strategies  so if you want a safe landing to make  sure that you can land get your weapons  your hacks  and make sure your team is together um  safely you can  all land straight down below or what we  were doing in the creator cup and in  other competitions where  we would land somewhat center of the map  that way we one could get on top of red  tiger  which is a location in the center to  offer kind of vantage points around  uh the entire map to see where straight  bullets are going or  if a team two teams are fighting to  where we can kind of get involved a  little bit early  i would recommend off the start  something with mobility especially in  these competitions where people are  being eliminated really really really  quick off the start  uh so teleport obviously closes the  distance can be used offensively or  defensively  slam you can basically pull yourself up  into the air  and it's really great for one like  looking around the entire map to see if  teams are fighting and you can see you  know a bird's eye view of where  everybody's at  and then you can secondly when you  complete your slam you slam down and do  extra damage to other players  invisibility is incredibly strong for if  you say get caught off guard so if you  get shot in the back  or kind of get caught off guard and  someone surprises you you can always  activate your invisibility and kind of  relocate reposition yourself  with eel heel offers really good sustain  when team fighting  there's quite a few matches where we ran  into other tournament teams  you know having that extra heel creates  that kind of sustain  to eventually win the fight or we could  relocate and reposition to give us a  better  chance to win the game obviously once  you get those core gameplay mechanics  honed and ready  you're gonna want to look into weapons  and hacks so  for you graeme what are some weapons and  hacks that you not only love to use  personally  but that you designed so for me in terms  of my favorite loadout i really  i'm a kind of short range player i like  to use the mammoth shotgun  which is really useful especially when  paired with teleport you can teleport up  be right on the player and shotgun them  at really close range secondly to that i  like to use the harpy harpy's kind of a  super fast rate  submachine gun same thing that's really  good when paired with  teleport or paired with invisibility  allows you to get up really close to  your enemy player and eliminate them  in terms of the weapons that we design  which i think are cool you know from dez  town  i really like the sky breaker it's  really interesting it fires this big  ball of energy you know you can see them  flying across the map and if you're good  enough to  land on someone it does a lot of damage  it's really interesting to see  these bolts fly towards you from other  rooftops and you're kind of dodging and  moving as you're shooting back at the  other players  and for you tanner have you noticed any  optimal loadouts or optimal combinations  that  really secure those tournament wins  personally i like to use  the ripper i've always been an assault  rifle player when it comes to fps games  so when you start out and you land  and get your core weapons of what you  want to level up when you find  duplicates of those weapons you can fuse  them together  majority of them you get magazine  increases and then on the final upgrade  you get a damage increase so it's really  crucial and important  to uh fuse the duplicates of your  loadout  uh to make them stronger and better so  primary i would say the ripper and then  myself  i really like using the riot one um  the damage output the more and more that  you level it up  uh is vital teleport and  like heal was a really good loadout to  run so the more and more that you fuse  the same thing goes along with your  hacks as well if you find the same hack  uh you can duplicate it to then reduce  the cooldown of your hack so you can  teleport more or heal your team more so  you know it's crucial to  find those duplicates now the game has  been  in the hands of the players for a little  bit over a week now  is there anything surprising that you've  seen the community  discover and learn or develop or any  tactics that you're shocked to see  i think two of the key things have been  really interesting one's people's usage  of wall  like we always thought about wall to  block someone in or to protect yourself  from behind  people are using it as a mobility hack  now as well they're throwing the wall on  the ground it teleports them up in the  air  and then they use that as mobility on  top so that's been really interesting  second one is the popularity of slam  like we knew slam was good  it allows you to be offensive or  defensive you can escape a gunfight by  projecting up in the air you can also  project up and slam down on an enemy but  it's been really really popular i think  it's almost in everybody's loadout so  that one's been really interesting to  see i think secondly to that is really  the popularity of the riot one pistol we  see a lot of players using  a sniper rifle for long-range tactics  but they also  seem to pair it with the riot one two so  they'll snipe the enemy a couple of  times or  once and then they'll finish them off  with the right one pistol so that one's  been super super popular as well  before you go green we wanted to finish  things off with something a little more  fun  and that was to collect some community  plays and get your reactions from it  because  we've seen some pretty cool stuff so far  so let's roll those clips  i see he's rocking the loadout the uh  the riot one mammoth  here's a good use of slime he's managed  to project himself up to the top of the  building and he's chased the player down  good slam right here to contest this  person on height he follows him down  with a mama's shotgun  stands right beside him has a good look  at him this player just has no  idea where he's at what's happening  around him  that was hilarious to see him just kind  of like looking around hopelessly like  i hope he doesn't know where i am you  know here this is a nice clip we 